    "body": "## Purpose\n\nMiniMax-M3-MXFP4 keeps the attention projections (fused q/k/v + index q/k, and o) in bf16; only the routed experts are MXFP4. This PR adds an **opt-in** switch, `VLLM_MINIMAX_M3_FP8_ATTN_PROJ=1`, that runs those projections through the existing online PTPC FP8 method (`Fp8PtpcOnlineLinearMethod`): per-output-channel FP8 weights quantized at load time and dynamic per-token FP8 activations. The routed experts keep the checkpoint's Quark MXFP4 config. It is off by default because it changes numerics.\n\n## Results (MI355X, MiniMax-M3-MXFP4 TP4, EAGLE3-GQA, golden AL 2.78)\n\nBase: `vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:nightly-rocm72-1b2a666391f2a24228a1436b64d547c34cc6b6ce`; this branch is based on the same commit and was tested as nightly + this patch with the flag on.\n\n**AgenticX C24** (InferenceX recipe `minimaxm3/vllm/mi355x-fp4-mtp/agentic.yaml`, `override_tp4_c24`, 3600 s replay of `semianalysisai/cc-traces-weka-062126`, one run each, same node):\n\n| | baseline | this PR | Δ |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Token throughput per chip | 24,920 | 25,136 | +0.87% |\n| Output throughput per chip | 180.2 | 180.7 | +0.28% |\n| Interactivity p50 | 52.1 | 52.7 | +0.98% |\n| TTFT p90 | 0.896 s | 0.868 s | −3.06% |\n| E2EL mean | 18.24 s | 17.97 s | −1.47% |\n\n**8k/1k C24** (240 requests, zero HTTP warmup, per-arm warmed compile caches, 2 interleaved rounds vs same-round baseline): output throughput **+2.44%** (+2.45 / +2.42), mean TTFT −5.8%, p99 E2EL −3.2%.\n\n**Where it comes from:** at prefill sizes the FP8 GEMMs are close to 2× the bf16 ones. In decode (M=96) the FP8 GEMMs save ~420 µs per step, but the two dynamic per-token quant kernels add ~500 µs, so a pure-decode step is ~1% slower; the end-to-end gain is prefill-driven. Fusing the qkv-input quant into the preceding RMSNorm (as other stacks do) should recover most of that decode cost and is a natural follow-up.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Real EAGLE3 (non-synthetic) correctness smoke with the flag on: 24 concurrent ≥8k-token prompts + 4 short requests, greedy, exact expected output — 24/24 and 4/4 pass.\n- Profiler trace confirms the q/k/v and o projections run FP8 GEMMs with per-token activation quant; experts unchanged.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format` clean.\n- **Not yet done:** an accuracy eval (e.g. GSM8K) with the flag on — required before considering making this a default.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
